        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Degenerate thermometers can fail product comparison",
        "statement": "The one-system order relation $U\\le U'$ on a degenerate thermometer state space $\\Gamma=(0,\\infty)$, together with the thermal equilibration operation described below, need not satisfy T4 or the comparison hypothesis on products. Consequently, a monotone entropy on the single-system space need not represent product accessibility.",
